WEBVTT

00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:21,100
But husband's HSCRP was elevated and what that means is high sensitivity, CE reactive protein or some labs call it cardiac CRP.

00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:33,100
And because when that fast test first came out, they thought it was going to be much more specific to cardiovascular issues.

00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:38,100
And you could argue that it probably is a little bit more specific to cardiovascular issues.

00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:44,100
But there's so many things that could cause elevated high sensitivity CRP.

00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:48,100
Any inflammation in your body could cause it. Certainly cardiac issues.

00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:56,100
Well, you could even have dental infections causing, you know, hidden dental infections causing elevated CRP.

00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:11,100
Brain inflammation could cause elevated CRP, Alzheimer's, Parkinson's, abdominal, you know, got issues can cause elevated CRP.

00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:18,100
Obesity can cause elevated CRP. There's a lot of things that can cause that. So investigating other things.

00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:23,100
Just like any lab marker, it's not a standalone thing.

00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:31,100
You have this, that means this. You have elevated PSA. That's pretty much means you have prostate cancer.

00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:37,100
Most markers aren't standalone. You have to look at it in conjunction with other things as well.

